0..75 Comment "//! A fold over each index of a family: it respects each rule at its index."
76..79 Comment "//!"
80..158 Comment "//! A family is one type at each index. A fold over the whole family takes the"
159..237 Comment "//! index as its first argument, and a rule of the family stands at one index."
238..302 Comment "//! The fold must give one answer on the two sides of each rule."
303..306 Comment "//!"
307..378 Comment "//! The checker stands the fold at the index that the root of each rule"
379..457 Comment "//! states. Each node of a side takes the index of its own constructor. A fold"
458..537 Comment "//! at one index owes nothing to a rule whose root stands at another index. The"
538..589 Comment "//! kernel decides each fold again by its own code."
590..593 Comment "//!"
594..610 Comment "//! - see: #8365"
611..690 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/desc/fold-over-family.gandr` — a fold that tells two"
691..718 Comment "//!   sides of a rule apart"
719..781 Comment "//! - see: `model/desc/family-with-rules.gandr` — the widths"
782..859 Comment "//! - see: `model/desc/fold-drops-variable.gandr` — a fold over a rule that"
860..882 Comment "//!   drops a variable"
884..895 Comment "// `Width`."
